commit 8fadd24043d92d4becd7607401fb37ec1ab15bad
Author: franckdjiongo <djiongoelly@yahoo.fr>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 11:36:56 2026 -0400

    fix(alerts): one bell entry per failure episode, stable across acknowledgment

    Round 2 of the adversarial review: marking an alert reminder done while the
    job still failed changed the bell id (it embedded only a PENDING reminder),
    so the front fired a second desktop notification for an acknowledged
    failure; a failure could also surface under two ids before/after the
    reminder was written. The bell entry now requires an alert reminder and
    embeds the task's most recent one whatever its status; alert reminders are
    left out of the bell's reminder items (one failure, one entry).

